{"id":"n5-132","title":"もう～ (mou～)","jlptLevel":5,"shortExplanation":"Expresses 'already', 'anymore', or 'soon'.","longExplanation":"The もう grammar point is used to express the idea of 'already', 'anymore', or 'soon' in English. It indicates that something has already happened, won't happen anymore, or will happen soon. It can be used with verbs, adjectives, or nouns depending on context.","formation":"もう + Verb / もう + Adjective / もう + Noun","examples":[{"jp":"もう昼ごはんを食べました。","romaji":"Mou hirugohan o tabemashita.","en":"I already ate lunch.","words":[{"surface":"もう","vocabId":"2081490","reading":"もう"},{"surface":"昼","vocabId":"1426250","reading":"ひる"},{"surface":"ごはん","vocabId":"1270590","reading":"ごはん"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"食べ","vocabId":"1358280","reading":"たべる"},{"surface":"まし","vocabId":null},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}]},{"jp":"もうここでは働かない。","romaji":"Mou koko de wa hatarakanai.","en":"I won't work here anymore.","words":[{"surface":"もう","vocabId":"2081490","reading":"もう"},{"surface":"ここ","vocabId":"1288810","reading":"ここ"},{"surface":"で","vocabId":null},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"働か","vocabId":"1451150","reading":"はたらく"},{"surface":"ない","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}]},{"jp":"もうすぐ夏休みですね。","romaji":"Mou sugu natsuyasumi desu ne.","en":"Summer vacation is coming soon, isn't it?","words":[{"surface":"もうすぐ","vocabId":null},{"surface":"夏休み","vocabId":"1191420","reading":"なつやすみ"},{"surface":"です","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ね","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}]},{"jp":"もう十分です。","romaji":"Mou juubun desu.","en":"It's already enough.","words":[{"surface":"もう","vocabId":"2081490","reading":"もう"},{"surface":"十分","vocabId":"1335080","reading":"じゅうぶん"},{"surface":"です","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}]}]}